/-!
# Regional algebras generated by source-local transition operators

Literal mirror of `docs/E1_SOURCE_OPERATOR_PAYLOAD.json` of
`oph-physics-sim` (schema `oph.sim.e1_source_operator_payload.v1`, payload
sha256 `98d17ab4683eb967acd3b420ea96c14f6130b7802a61e7ef56561ef8f413ca6c`,
extracted post hoc from the retained gates-passing rich-fibre bundle
`runs/e1_prereg2_64k_20260810`): for each of the four committed rich
observers, the 32-step support-modal label path over the five packet
fields, the realized state alphabet, the counted transition operator, and
the field projectors.

The mathematical content is the adapter-preflight generation theorem the
completion plan names for E1: the star-algebra generated by one
observer's counted transition operator together with its diagonal field
projectors is the **full matrix algebra** on its realized alphabet.  The
proof route is reachability: the field projectors separate the realized
states (kernel-decided), so every diagonal matrix unit is a product of
projectors; compressing the transition operator between two diagonal
units extracts each counted step as a matrix unit; and the committed walk
visits every realized state, so products and adjoints of step units reach
every matrix unit.  A diagonal-only negative control proves that the
projectors alone stay inside the diagonal algebra, so the transition
operator is load-bearing.

**Boundary.**  The state alphabet, walk, and counts are post-hoc
transcriptions of committed run outputs; the extraction was not
preregistered and is ineligible as validation.  The generated algebras
replace the declared pair-groupoid enrichment of the earlier packet at
the level of one observer's realized label space; no region lattice,
restriction system, tensor factorisation, physical channel, instrument,
or prediction is constructed here.  Issue #692 stays open.
-/

